# A design that names its sources and tools. Synthetic: the clinicians, patients
# and volumes are invented, and the tools it names are local stand-ins.

@meta
use_case: For each of about 40 appointments a day, decide whether the patient needs a pre-visit chase and draft the wording for a clinician to approve
author: process-to-loop, as a worked example
date: 2026-10-05
approver: A. Clinician, attending
exit_criterion: Shut down if 1 or more flagged submissions are closed without a clinician reading them, or if the drafted wording is found to contain 1 or more patient identifiers, in 2 consecutive weeks

@assumptions
- Synthetic. No real clinician, patient or appointment in this design is from a real practice.
- The intake submission carries a flag the triage rule needs; nothing else from the form is required to decide.
- A clinician approves every drafted note before it reaches a patient, so the model never sends anything.

@unit
definition: one appointment on the day's list
kind: rule
fanout: 40
fanout_reason: about 40 appointments a day on one clinician's list
thinking_justification: two, and they are different jobs. Step 4 drafts wording from redacted fields and decides nothing. Step 6 is the judgment: a clinician decides whether this patient is chased at all, which no rule in this process settles.

@steps
1 | pull appointments | mechanical | code | read the day's appointments from the appointment service | batch
2 | pull submissions | mechanical | code | read today's intake submissions | batch
3 | redact | mechanical | code | keep the flag and the form name, drop patient_ref and every other identifier | unit
4 | draft chase wording | thinking | model | from the redacted fields alone, draft what the chase note should say | unit
5 | scan the draft | test | code | check the drafted wording against the identifier list | unit
6 | clinician approves | thinking | human | the clinician approves the wording, edits it, or declines the chase | unit
7 | record the decision | test | code | confirm an approval row exists for this appointment before anything is sent | unit

@gates
4 | the submission is flagged and 0 clinicians have read it | send it to the on-call clinician before any wording is drafted
5 | the drafted wording contains 1 or more patient identifiers | return it to step 3 and redact again
7 | more than 0 chases are sent without an approval recorded | stop the run and tell the attending

@sources
appointments | eb-appointment-service | appointment_id, patient_ref, status | -
intake-forms | eb-form-builder-service | submission_id, flagged | never reaches a model

@tools
eb-appointment-service | 1 | read the day's appointments
eb-form-builder-service | 2 | read today's intake submissions

@evidence
writer_step: 3
integrity: sha256 over the redacted payload and the drafted wording
proof: the redacted payload that was handed to step 4, beside what came back

@record
transitions: every step change for every appointment, appended
units: one row per appointment with its outcome and the approving clinician
retention: 7 years
acceptance: the clinician who approved the wording, with a timestamp

@kpis
cost per appointment | cost | unmeasured
clinician edits per draft | quality | unmeasured
appointments handled per day | throughput | 40
clinician minutes returned | tvr-speed | unmeasured
